  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `.claude/skills/merge-ready/SKILL.md`: the maintainer's local merge-ready skill, ported step for step (preconditions, collect, plan, ask in groups, wave 1, wave 2 one at a time, after-merge sweeps, report, one gate per batch). Every planner call is `cargo xtask merge-plan ...`; no home-directory path. Safety rules kept: the user decides, never merge an unapproved PR, never `gh pr review --approve`, merge commits only, fork branches are not deleted, stacked children retargeted first, refresh only the PR that is next in the batch.\n- Planner (`xtask/src/merge_plan*.rs`): every order choice is a named total order ending in the PR number (`wave1_pick_key`, `order_key`, `wave2_key`, `shared_first`); repeated PR numbers resolve by (number, head); a shared-history pair keyed either way round reads the same; the simulated-commit cache is a `BTreeMap`. The plan prints the full base sha and each PR's head sha. New `--json` (waves, order, per-PR kind, conflicted files, shas, `after`). Rendering moved to `merge_plan_out.rs` (files stay under 400 lines).\n- Scope change from the maintainer (question dialog, 2026-11-12: \"Any collaborator review counts\", \"Both collaborators\" may merge; chat: \"everyone counts. everyone needs to get merged, mkinney and i are coolaboration across the world on the same code base\"): markers and `merge-ready` labels count when made by a collaborator (push permission), not only the owner; any collaborator's session runs `/merge-ready` and merges, cuts/tags stay with the maintainer; non-collaborators' PRs still wait for the user. Updated in AGENTS.md (the #1227 rule kept as \"Superseded since 2026-11-12, later the same day\"), review-prs, resolve-conflicts, PR-reviewer and the new skill. `xtask` reads no marker author, so no code change there.\n- AGENTS.md also names `/merge-ready` as how a batch is run (in \"Outside PRs are reviewed\"). `PROCESS_VERSION` 31 -> 32.\n\n## Parity with the reference planner (`plan_merge_order.py`)\n\n| Behaviour | Status |\n|---|---|\n| Stack ordering (child's base is parent's branch, or parent head is an ancestor) | same |\n| Shared unmerged history: fewer own commits first | same; a tie now goes explicitly to the lower number (as the reference's `<=` on sorted numbers) |\n| Wave-1 selection (fewest live rivals, fewest paths) | same, with the number as last key, as the reference |\n| Merge order: docs first, hot files last, small before large | same, number last |\n| Wave-2 order and kinds (clean after wave 1 / mechanical / by hand) | same |\n| GitHub-only conflict = `plain refresh` (git clean, GitHub CONFLICTING, several merge bases) | same |\n| UNKNOWN mergeable: 6 x 5 s retries, then a WARNING line, planned as git says | same |\n| Octopus merge in `--delta` = NEW CODE | same |\n| `--delta` classes SAME / MECHANICAL / DELTA / NEW CODE | same |\n| Base sha | differs: printed in full (reference printed 8 chars) so two runs compare |\n| Head shas, `--json` | new (reference had no head shas; its `--json` had no per-PR sha or kind) |\n| Scratch refs `refs/merge-plan/N` | differs: deleted after the run (the reference left them) |\n| Reference was Python | differs: Rust, so it runs on every OS with the workspace and is unit-tested without git |\n\n## How tested\n\n- `cargo test -p xtask`: 88 passed. Pinning tests in `xtask/src/merge_plan_det_tests.rs`: `shuffled_input_gives_the_identical_plan` (an 8-PR fixture with docs, hot, stacked, pair clashes, base conflict, shared history, GitHub-only and UNKNOWN; 23 input orders; plan, text and JSON all identical), `a_repeated_pr_number_resolves_the_same_way_in_either_order`, `wave1_tie_on_rivals_and_paths_goes_to_the_lower_number`, `wave1_fewer_rivals_beats_fewer_paths_and_number`, `wave1_fewer_paths_beats_the_number`, `merge_order_is_docs_then_cool_then_hot_then_small_then_number`, `wave2_order_is_parents_then_fewest_files_then_number`, `shared_history_tie_goes_to_the_lower_number_and_either_key_direction_reads_the_same`, `unknown_list_is_in_number_order_whatever_the_input_order`, `output_names_the_base_and_every_head`, `json_escapes_quotes_backslashes_and_control_characters`. No real git in the unit tests.\n- `cargo clippy -p xtask --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean. `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: green on the first run.\n- Planner run twice each against live PRs (read-only, it only fetches): `cargo xtask merge-plan 1319 1314 1311 1310` printed the identical plan both times (base 4ea96bd5; wave 1 #1319, #1314; wave 2 #1310 by hand in `xtask/src/main.rs`, #1311 mechanical on `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION`). `--label merge-ready`: the first run (base 8e9489e2) planned #1134 alone; by the time of the paired runs no open PR carried the label, and both runs gave the same clean \"no matching open PRs\" error. Main moved between those runs, which is why the base sha is printed.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe skill was not run end to end on a real merge. `--json` with `--delta` is not defined (`--delta` prints its class as text).\n\n## Process announcement for #681\n\n`PROCESS_VERSION 32` · PR #<this> · the merge-ready skill is now in the repo (`.claude/skills/merge-ready/`) and `cargo xtask merge-plan` is deterministic with head shas and `--json`; **this reverses PROCESS_VERSION 31's \"only the owner's reviews count\"**: a review marker or `merge-ready` label now counts when a collaborator (push permission) made it, and any collaborator's session may merge PRs that meet the rule (cuts and tags stay with the maintainer); non-collaborators' markers still do not count. A fork must pull the process files (`AGENTS.md`, `.claude/agents`, `.claude/skills`, `.claude/PROCESS_VERSION`, `xtask`).\n\nEffort: medium. No `push`, `pull_request` or `schedule` trigger added.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #1320\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
